// the container has to have storage the write can reach. as an assignment target this was refused by the
// ownership pass; as a call operand a temporary would merely be bound for the statement, and the write
// would land in a map destroyed at the end of it - so the refusal moved with the rule
function make() : map<string, int32>
{
    map<string, int32> $m = map<string, int32>();

    return $m;
}

make()['a'] = 1;
